      <p>Effective Date: May 12, 2026 | Last Updated: May 12, 2026</p>
      <p>This notice discloses how Don't Lose Your Way, operated by CC3PO LLC (CA LLC, EIN 33-2353877), uses artificial intelligence. California law (AB 853, AB 2013, and AB 316) requires businesses to be transparent about AI use.</p>
      <h1>What AI We Use</h1>
      <h3>AI Songwriting Generator</h3>
      <p>Our songwriting feature uses AI to generate song lyrics based on your text prompts. You provide a mood, theme, or idea, and AI creates lyrics in English, Spanish, or Spanglish. This is creative content generation — not therapy, counseling, or mental health advice.</p>
      <h3>Chapel Reflections</h3>
      <p>The Chapel feature may use AI to generate mood-based reflections or prompts. These are creative exercises for personal reflection — not therapeutic interventions or clinical recommendations.</p>
      <h2>What AI Does NOT Do</h2>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>AI does not provide mental health diagnosis or treatment.</strong> It generates creative content, not clinical recommendations</li>
      <li><strong>AI does not make autonomous decisions about your mental health.</strong> Per California AB 316, no AI on this platform makes consequential decisions about you</li>
      <li><strong>AI does not replace professional help.</strong> If you are struggling, please reach out to a qualified mental health professional or crisis line</li>
      <li><strong>AI-generated content may be inaccurate or unhelpful.</strong> It is generated based on patterns, not understanding of your specific situation</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How Your Data Is Handled</h2>
      <ul>
      <li>Text you enter for songwriting or reflections is sent to AI providers for processing</li>
      <li>We instruct AI providers not to use your data for model training</li>
      <li>AI processing is temporary — text is processed and results are returned</li>
      <li>We do not store your prompts or AI outputs on our servers unless you choose to save them locally</li>
      <li>Journal entries are stored in your browser's local storage, not on our servers</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>California AI Law Compliance</h2>
      <h3>AB 853 — AI Transparency</h3>
      <p>We disclose that AI is used on this platform, what it does, and its limitations. This notice is our compliance with California's AI transparency requirements.</p>
      <h3>AB 2013 — Training Data Disclosure</h3>
      <p>AI services used on this platform have their own training data practices. We do not contribute your input to AI training datasets. For details about their training data, refer to their respective transparency reports.</p>
      <h3>AB 316 — Autonomous Decision Prohibition</h3>
      <p>No AI system on this platform makes autonomous consequential decisions. All AI-generated content — songs, reflections, and prompts — is creative and advisory. You always decide what to do with it.</p>
      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Right to know:</strong> You have the right to know when AI is processing your input</li>
      <li><strong>Right to opt out:</strong> You can choose not to use AI features. The Chapel and journal are available without AI generation</li>
      <li><strong>Right to report:</strong> If AI generates harmful, biased, or concerning content, please contact us</li>
      <li><strong>Right to deletion:</strong> Since we don't store your prompts on our servers, there's nothing to delete. Journal entries can be cleared from your browser</li>
      </ul>
